Message-ID: <nnskvbURjJo.IEZmjr-2AAAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <nnskvbURjJo.Q5r9koStAAAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <nnskvbURjJo.Q5r9koStAAAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl2-disc/c/nnskvbURjJo/m/IEZmjr-2AAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Markers need to have the same chromosome identifiers on the genetic maps that are used on the physical maps. The markers also need to be in the exact same order. The only difference between the two maps is that positions are in cM on the genetic map and in Mbp on the physical maps.

karl

